course: dictionary
lesson: 12236
title: Consign: sending away for good
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Consign is a formal word, the kind you meet in older stories, history books and exam texts. It means to send something away, or to put it somewhere, often so that it is out of the way for good. The words around it give you the clues.
explain: «The broken chairs were consigned to the bin.» Rubbish goes in a bin, and nobody wants broken chairs. So consigned means put away or thrown out, and the sentence suggests they will not be used again.
explain: Consign can also mean handing something over to someone's care: «Mum consigned the baby to her aunt for the afternoon.» Swap in gave or handed over and the sentence still makes sense, so that is the meaning here.
fact: «Consign» means to send something away, or put it in a place, often to get rid of it.
fact: «Consign» can mean to send goods to someone, often to be sold or delivered.
fact: «Consign to history» means to make something belong to the past and be forgotten.
fact: «Consign» can also mean to hand something over to someone's care.
fact: Consigned, consigns and consigning are all forms of the same word.
exercise: «The broken radio was consigned to the scrapheap.» What does consigned mean here? | Carried home carefully | Played loudly | *Put away and thrown out | Mended by an expert
exercise: Dad reads in a history book: «The old king was consigned to history.» What does this suggest? | He became a teacher | He wrote a very long letter | *He was forgotten, as part of the past | He still rules the country today
exercise: Which word in «The nurse consigned the puppy to the vet for the night» means handed over to someone's care? | *consigned | night | nurse | puppy
test: «The shop consigned fifty boxes of tea to the port for shipping.» What does consigned mean here? | Hidden under the counter | Counted twice | Drunk quickly | *Sent off to be delivered
test: Ella's mum says, «I will consign you to Grandma while I work.» What does consign mean here? | *Hand you over to Grandma's care | Teach you to cook | Throw you away | Shout at you
exam: «Once the plan failed, the team consigned it to the past and never spoke of it again.» What does consigned it to the past suggest? | They read it aloud to everyone | They posted it to another team | They made it bigger and better | *They forgot it and put it aside for good
